cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ULTR-AI, please cite the version-specific software release and
  the associated research article below.
title: "ULTR-AI: Ultrasound-led TB Recognition Using AI"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Brokowski
    given-names: Trevor
    affiliation: "Laboratory for Intelligent Global Health and Humanitarian Response Technologies (LiGHT), EPFL"
abstract: >-
  ULTR-AI is research software for developing and evaluating artificial
  intelligence models that analyze lung ultrasound for pulmonary tuberculosis
  triage. The codebase supports direct image-to-TB prediction, prediction of
  human-recognizable lung ultrasound signs, patient-level aggregation, and
  evaluation against study outcome labels.
repository-code: "https://github.com/tbrokowski/UltrAI"
url: "https://github.com/tbrokowski/UltrAI"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - deep learning
  - diagnostic accuracy
  - global health
  - lung ultrasound
  - medical imaging
  - point-of-care ultrasound
  - tuberculosis
  - triage
